{"id": "EUVD-2026-59730", "enisaUuid": "e5bea8d0-406e-35db-9ebe-0184e2a2e5e2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: hold sk properly in iso_conn_ready\n\nsk deref in iso_conn_ready must be done either under conn->lock, or\nholding a refcount, to avoid concurrent close. conn->sk is currently\naccessed without either:\n\n    [Task 1]            [Task 2]\n                        iso_sock_release\n    iso_conn_ready\n      sk = conn->sk\n                          lock_sock(sk)\n                            conn->sk = NULL\n      lock_sock(sk)\n                          release_sock(sk)\n                          iso_sock_kill(sk)\n       UAF on sk deref\n\nFix possible UAF by holding sk refcount in iso_conn_ready().  Also\nrecheck after lock_sock that the socket is still valid.  Adjust locking\nso conn->sk is cleared only under lock_sock.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T12:27:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:50", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/44590dc53c9e949d2fed399a571a89c3d7d0b245", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/99b65f0ea3370c13687ff870330c425b6ca44e89", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4e9b5e8669b3602a4e01b6d1e9539b72e42c84d5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1308d72903d792d10b82bc4ef08b8a4452308b04", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0d255e63fcf3f13a570d7ac11678fa1164ac015c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74537", "GHSA-4f56-g5vg-w2cg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "058de789-d60d-35b6-a0d9-9f8ed9436669", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27c24fda62b601d6f9ca5e992502578c4310876f <44590dc53c9e949d2fed399a571a89c3d7d0b245"}, {"id": "107033f6-b916-3034-9ccb-e9699cf2a207", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.8"}, {"id": "1a1dd3e3-7839-3e7c-ad35-e2eebe5b3b10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27c24fda62b601d6f9ca5e992502578c4310876f <1308d72903d792d10b82bc4ef08b8a4452308b04"}, {"id": "1f050089-338b-3ee4-b7b6-1b8add4d0dc9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "632b05ae-ead4-3030-9d49-3e1fde7ba0bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "68232c23-6853-3b6e-b3cf-5524834cd737", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "75665235-a757-3f78-bdf6-41d7b651dd4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9fa0032e-160a-35aa-9197-ff05b1a1e08b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27c24fda62b601d6f9ca5e992502578c4310876f <0d255e63fcf3f13a570d7ac11678fa1164ac015c"}, {"id": "cba6d451-abc7-3a21-a057-1da1105ab90a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.44"}, {"id": "d6b37a16-699c-375a-9b98-c744012d58ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "e0818dfc-41c0-338f-ba20-6872c2daa946", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27c24fda62b601d6f9ca5e992502578c4310876f <99b65f0ea3370c13687ff870330c425b6ca44e89"}, {"id": "f8632a60-745b-3466-9fb3-3cdf48c87db6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27c24fda62b601d6f9ca5e992502578c4310876f <4e9b5e8669b3602a4e01b6d1e9539b72e42c84d5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f96e0285-06c5-3e52-b92d-58221e04b1b4", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}